+## 6. Limitations and notes
+
+- **llvmpipe only.** Every frame, timing and test ran on the software rasteriser; none of it says anything about the
+  Victus or any GPU.
+- **The disk was full.** The container's root file system had about 270 MB free for the whole stage; the clone, the
+  work folder and the canonical captures lived on a RAM disk (`/dev/shm/ram/...`: the clone behind
+  `/home/user/g2w/polish3`, the captures behind the scratchpad's `captures/polish-3/` link, which the orchestrator
+  prepared). They survive only as long as the container runs: the committed review JPEGs and the bundle are the
+  durable record.
+- **A capture run discarded.** The first canonical run started on c2bb0d6; two later code changes (the prisoner search
+  in finer rings and the stronger arm laying, both from the tests) would have left C and D on older code, so I stopped
+  it after A and part of B and started the whole set again on b781165. Every capture in §2 is from that run; since
+  b781165 only tests, scripts and documents changed (no runtime code).
+- **The golden-hour hue target is not met.** The critic asked for a far band of hue 80–160 at golden hour; it measures
+  36–37 (as before) because the far land in those shots is seen towards a low sun through a warm glow (§1, rank 1). The
+  glow and its brightness are lower (far/near luma 2.28 → 1.73 in the vista), and the band reads as dark olive land in a
+  warm haze rather than a beige plain, but it is not green. A greener far land at low sun would need the aerial
+  perspective's forward scattering cut further than looks right for the sky above it.
+- **Not worked:** the crowd LOD re-bake with locked borders (the bake writes the shared asset folder that other clones
+  read; a re-bake into a new folder needs a loader change I did not make); hero characters for the nearest crowd
+  soldiers; side and curled death poses and a relaxation of the bodies themselves (they still overlap: the polish2
+  settle is unchanged); skin pores, cavity, beard root occlusion, brow and lash cards, hands; a sparse heap layer at low
+  sun; the river's shoreline, water colour by depth, reeds in clumps and triplanar banks; broken merlons, rubble,
+  villagers, paths and pens; the output dither (it would move pixel-exact test references by one step; the far terraces
+  came from the ring geometry, which is fixed).
+- **Hearth smoke is in every bench scene with the village** (B, C, D, E), not only E: the village plan is shared.
+- **Scene D's victors stand without their spears** (a crowd view with the shield and without the weapon): with the
+  spears held level at the hip they passed through the men beside them; nothing lies at their feet in their place.
+
+## 7. Reproduce
+
+```
+cd prototypes/m7-gfx2
+dotnet build M7Gfx2.slnx -c Release -m:1 -nodeReuse:false
+scripts/capture-scenes.sh OUT_DIR                                      # 1920x1080, 8 samples; + avatar triptych, motion
+scripts/review-sheets-polish3.py BEFORE_DIR OUT_DIR SHEETS_DIR REVIEW_DIR
+scripts/measure-polish3.py BEFORE_DIR OUT_DIR                          # the figures of §1 marked "capture"
+dotnet test Gfx.Tests/Gfx.Tests.csproj -c Release --no-build --filter "FullyQualifiedName~Gfx.Tests.Polish3Tests"
+dotnet Gfx.Demo/bin/Release/net10.0/Gfx.Demo.dll --suite smoke --out DIR   # llvmpipe costs, slots A-E
+```
